<section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="s1-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__aside">
        <h2 class="split__title rv" id="s1-title">Protect Your Organization From Impersonation, Synthetic Identities and Deepfake Fraud</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body prose">
        <p class="rv">Businesses have long relied on a face, a voice or a document to decide who to trust. AI has made all three cheap to fake. A cloned voice can ask finance for an urgent transfer, a generated face can open a bank account, and a convincing caller can talk a help desk into resetting a password.</p>
        <p class="rv">CipherTrivia's digital identity and deepfake security services test those weak points the way a determined attacker would. We examine your onboarding and identity verification, login and recovery flows, voice and call-center checks, help desk procedures and payment approvals, then show where a fake could get through.</p>
        <p class="rv">Every simulation is authorized, uses consenting participants or synthetic personas and follows agreed rules of engagement. The result is a clear list of fixes that combine technical controls with practical process changes, so trust does not depend on how convincing someone looks or sounds.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

